schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "Polished writing is not automatically reviewed knowledge"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    "Polished writing is not automatically reviewed knowledge" — readers
    cannot distinguish a beautifully written unreviewed draft from a
    fact-checked, reviewed page unless the review state is explicitly labelled.
  evidence: >-
    Named as one of the Regen Web3 Toolkit's own cross-cutting principles
    (Maturity and review state), illustrated by the article's opening example
    of a confident-looking but unreviewed treasury-payout page.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/review-and-maturity.md
  interpretation: >-
    Argues for mandatory, visible maturity labelling (not just internal
    metadata) as the cheap fix — a badge at the top of the page, not a
    footnote.
  uncertainty: >-
    Editorial/design guidance rather than an empirically tested claim; the
    treasury-payout scenario is illustrative, not a documented incident.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/review-and-maturity.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
